contentText:
After months of back-and-forth, two planned stadium gigs by Ye at Gazprom Arena in St. Petersburg, Russia have reportedly been canceled. Ye (formerly Kanye West ) was slated to perform on Oct. 10 and 11 at the venue, though the reportedly sold-out shows were in question from the time they were announced.

On Aug. 24, the venue posted on social media that the 80,000-capacity stadium &#8220; did not sign any contracts for the stadium rent for the event.&#8221; The post adamantly stated that there was &#8220;no such agreement&#8221; for the shows and that they would not take place at the venue. That came despite the venue hyping the shows on Instagram just a week earlier.

